{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/347097-lots-of-hunters","id":347097,"title":"Lots Of Hunters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-21T19:10:45-08:00","id":347097,"title":"Lots Of Hunters","content":"How does one create a bunch of hunters as NPCs? For instance I want 20 hunters at my disposal. Do I have to make up 20 character sheets to keep track of stats or is there an easier way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4580-julian-weston","name":"Julian Weston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4580_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T21:22:47-08:00","id":347152,"title":"","content":"The thing is do you really need so closely specified hunters? Just think what are the relevant traits you might need to roll for them, likely Physical stats and Brawl/Melee/Athletics if meant as antagonists and if meant as allies why would you need specific traits for them instead of just having generic capability at certain things reflecting their personalities.<br /> <br /> Basically all you need is a name, description, and generalization of those stats you are likely to roll. If meant to be short time antagonists or random mooks, as perhaps suggested by the sheer number of them, you might not even need that much easily dropping the name away and giving general description instead of anything specific.<br /> <br /> Example.<br /> <br /> Chris Redfield, Experienced Hunter<br /> Physicals 3<br /> Brawl, Melee, Athletics 3<br /> WP 6<br /> Courage 4<br /> <br /> Natalie Summers, inexperienced hunter (or just more of a researcher type)<br /> Physicals 2<br /> Brawl, Melee, Athletics 1<br /> WP 6<br /> Courage 2<br /> <br /> Random Mook<br /> Attack 3 dice<br /> Dodge 3 dice<br /> Soak (if relevant often you wont need even soak scores for mooks) 2B/0L<br /> <br /> etc.<br /> <br /> Only make full character sheet type NPC's of those who are likely to be recurring Major NPC's. Fudge the stats according to the level of challenge you want your hunters to be if they are a group of very experienced hunters, or just ex-military spec ops, you can set even mooks at 4-5 dice attacks and dodge while the individual meaningful members might have physicals at 4 along with relevant combat stats at 4 as well for a attack/defensive pool of 8 etc.<br /> <br /> If they are not meant as antagonists the PC's are gonna fight against then it's more important to have their descriptions, names and personalities than any specific stats, and should you suddenly need such stats grant them a pool according to their history/personality and mark that down for future reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T10:16:25-08:00","id":347514,"title":"","content":"Stat fully those who are in the charge of operation, those who serve as rank and files you should represent with one sheet, for comparison look how NPCs in V20 like Criminal Enforcers and Government Agents are statted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T20:48:30-08:00","id":348769,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the help. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4580-julian-weston","name":"Julian Weston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4580_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}